 "result_text": "I added `\"swimlane\"` to `UserStory.allowed_params` in `taiga/models/models.py`. I haven't run any tests or tried it against a Taiga server.\n\n`update()` only sends the fields listed in `allowed_params`, and `swimlane` wasn't on the list. So `story.update()` never sent the story's current swimlane, and the server treated the missing field as \"no swimlane\". That would explain the move to Unclassified. It would also explain why setting `story.swimlane = <id>` appeared to do nothing: the new value was never included in the request.\n\nWith the field listed, `update()` should now send the swimlane. A status change keeps the story in its lane, and assigning a swimlane id should work.\n\nI also didn't check whether `UserStory` objects loaded from the API carry a `swimlane` attribute. If some responses omit it, `update()` still wouldn't send it for those stories.",
